# Milk Bread Recipes — Zojirushi BB-HAC10

Both recipes use the **SOFT** course (3:00). Crust control isn't available on SOFT. Don't use the delay timer — both contain milk.

## General steps

1. Seat the kneading blade first: line up the flat side of the hole with the flat side of the shaft and push it all the way down. Turning the blade by hand should turn the shaft.
2. Add ingredients in the order listed: liquids first, then flour, sugar, salt and butter, with the yeast last.
3. Put the yeast in a small well in the center of the flour so it stays dry until mixing starts. Cut the butter into a few pieces.
4. Lock the pan in by turning it clockwise toward LOCK. Close the lid, press MODE SELECT until the arrow is on SOFT, then press START/RESET.
5. Ignore the ADD beep (about 30 min in), since there are no add-ins.
6. When it's done, remove the pan right away and turn out the loaf. Let it cool completely (1 hour or more) before slicing.

